**Summary:**




 Sciente Group is a multi\-award winning, ISO9001/Great Place to Work/Personal Data Protection Trustmark/ISO27001 certified, Singapore headquartered technology focused organisation with business interest in Singapore (HQ), USA, Malaysia, Philippines and India.










**Currently, we are expanding our India tech recruitment consulting team to support our APAC business growth of business technology consulting, DATA \& AI solutions, and tech talent services.** 










 Our mission: Delighted clients \& community.




 Our employee value proposition: Learning \& Development, Career Growth and Sincere \& Approachable leadership.




 Therefore we promise a stable long\-term career growth for you.










**What is expected from this role to start with?**









* **Build and manage a team of TAs for APAC region and to ensure the desired key performance indicators (KPIs) are achieved by the team on a monthly basis**
* Team members must follow a consultative approach to understand the on\-site IT job role requirements \& expectations we have in Asia Pacific (APAC);
* Understand various technologies involved in the role and how it works;
* Derive an effective sourcing strategy to reach out to right group of tech talents within the APAC country of job role;
* Understand the matching skills/capabilities/aspirations of the tech talents;
* Guide talents for their career progression in a consultative manner (candidate management);
* Work closely with on\-site client facing managers/business development managers;
* Present the right talent profiles to the clients or client facing managers;
* Own\-up and build good rapport/relationship with the shortlisted candidates through out the process;
* Manage shortlisted candidates proactively with a consultative approach;
* Facilitate the matching/hiring process for the client to hire the right talents, bingo! That's what is expected from this role.









**Who shall fit\-in the best for this role?**









* Relevant work experience of 10 years in executive search or IT talent acquisition or tech recruitment in client servicing environment shall be needed;
* **At least 3 years of recent work experience of leading a team for Singapore, Malaysia, Philippines clients is a "MUST";**
* **You must have a proven track record in leading a productive team of consultants serving APAC region** 
 ;
* Communication, inter\-personal skills, meticulous and result\-orientation are the most important attributes for this role;
* Having a mind\-set of delivering value to make candidates/clients succeed and commitment to the purpose of the role;
* Positive attitude to put\-in efforts to achieve the desired goals shall make you a good fit for this role;
* Education in engineering or computer science related discipline shall be highly desired;
* This being a tech specialised role, ability to keep learning is one of the key success factors for this role.









 Should you be interested in this opportunity, please send in your updated resume to HR@sciente.com at the earliest. To know more, please visit https://www.sciente.com










 When you apply, you voluntarily consent to the disclosure, collection and use of your personal data for employment/recruitment and related purposes in accordance with the SCIENTE Group Privacy Policy, a copy of which is published at SCIENTE’s website (https://www.sciente.com/privacy\-policy).










 Confidentiality is assured, and only shortlisted candidates will be notified for interviews.

The Service Manager, South India is responsible for leading and driving service operations, customer experience, and service business growth for the Medical Solutions business across South India. The incumbent will ensure operational excellence, profitable service delivery, strong customer satisfaction, effective distributor management, and the achievement of service revenue and business objectives while maintaining high standards of quality and compliance.










**Key Responsibilities** 



* Manage day\-to\-day service operations and ensure achievement of service KPIs and business objectives;
* Drive customer satisfaction through timely, high\-quality service support and issue resolution;
* Lead service revenue growth through service contracts, repairs, and other service offerings;
* Monitor and improve service processes, SOP compliance, and operational efficiency;
* Oversee service center performance, ensuring quality standards and turnaround time (TAT) targets are met;
* Manage service budgets, forecasts, costs, and profitability;
* Build and maintain strong relationships with customers, distributors, and key stakeholders;
* Monitor installed base (IB) coverage, service contract renewal rates, and service business performance;
* Ensure effective use of service systems and tools, including SFDC, for reporting and performance tracking;
* Conduct regular reviews of service quality and implement continuous improvement initiatives;
* Lead, coach, and develop the service team to achieve individual and team goals;
* Support regional service projects and new business initiatives as required;
* Ensure compliance with company policies, regulatory requirements, and quality standards.









**Qualifications:** 



* Bachelor's degree in Electronics Engineering, Medical Science, Technology, or a related field preferred.
* Minimum 5 years of experience in the medical device industry preferred.
* Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with proficiency in the local language, Hindi, and/or English.
* Demonstrated ability to develop and execute effective sales strategies.
* Proficiency in CRM software and sales analytics tools.
* Ability to thrive in a fast\-paced, dynamic environment.









 If you believe you meet these qualifications, I encourage you to apply for the role.

**Way of Working**

 \-

 Full time Office role (Bangalore)










**YOE :** 
 4\-7 years.










**About Swiggy**










 Swiggy is India’s leading on\-demand delivery platform with a tech\-first approach to logistics and a solution\-first approach to consumer demands. With a presence in 500\+ cities across India, partnerships with hundreds of thousands of restaurants, an employee base of over 5000, a 2 lakh\+ strong independent fleet of Delivery Executives, we deliver unparalleled convenience driven by continuous innovation. Built on the back of robust ML technology and fueled by terabytes of data processed every day, Swiggy offers a fast, seamless and reliable delivery experience for millions of customers across India.




 From starting out as a hyperlocal food delivery service in 2014, to becoming India’s leading on\-demand convenience platform today, our capabilities result not only in lightning\-fast delivery for customers, but also in a productive and fulfilling experience for our employees.










**Roles \& Responsibilities:**










 ● Facilitate acquisition of compliance certificates and registrations;




 ● Audit and implement compliance policies.




 ● Support legal and business stakeholders on a variety of compliance issues and transactions, including, potential conflicts of interest, high\-risk payments, appropriate segregation of duties, and audit and report compliance with the statutory compliance matters;




 ● Organize and deliver compliance training and communications in integrity and compliance culture;




 ● Be a key contributor to developing and implementing new compliance policies;




 ● Strong interfacing with internal auditors to address significant matters.











 Desired Skills:











 ● Proven work experience post LLB in compliance function, including audit, risk assessment, and mitigation;




 ● Suitable maturity, judgment, and expertise when addressing compliance\-related issues and dealing with both internal and external clients;




 ● Ability to work across diverse and cross\-functional teams;




 ● Well conversant with applicable laws with special emphasis on understanding food laws, food industry laws, logistics, and e\-commerce related laws and compliance, internet and technology\-related laws, and laws regarding software as a service.




 ● Professional Qualifications: A bachelor of Laws is a must; added diplomas in compliance\-related courses would be an added bonus.










 We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by the law.

Godrej \& Boyce Mfg. Co. Ltd. ( G\&B ), a part of the Godrej Enterprises Group, has played a key role in India’s economic history by driving excellence in design and manufacturing and delivering sustainable value for its stakeholders and communities.




 Godrej Enterprises Group's diverse presence across 10 industries \- from complex engineering solutions to consumer goods like storage solutions, furniture and security solutions \- positively impacts the lives of one\-third of India's population every day.




 Through international subsidiaries and joint ventures, the company's products have also established a strong global footprint across 5 continents.




 As a value\-driven company known for its integrity and strong social conscience, it has built a compassionate corporate culture designed to empower the individuals, teams and communities that the Godrej Enterprises operates in. For this, Godrej Enterprises has been consistently recognized as one of India's most respected companies. Our focus on customers for over a century has helped us constantly innovate; design products and solutions with clarity of purpose that are manufactured in a quality\-driven and technology\- led environment and distributed through a national and international network of partners. Strong sustainable practices that help protect the environment are also enshrined in our Good \& Green policy that remains at the core of Godrej Enterprise Group’s business operations.










**Job Profile:\-**










**Key Responsibility Areas\-** 



* Conducting legal due diligence and advising the business team on the title in respect of properties Pan India;
* Advising business teams on real estate transactions, including residential and commercial properties;
* Drafting Real Estate transaction documents, either to sell/ purchase the property or lease/ license of the properties; and
* Preparing Dashboard summary of the transaction status update and the way forward.









**Job** 
**Description\-** 



* Conducting legal due diligence for verifying the title of seller or lessor or licensor of the property before commencement of the transaction;
* Providing legal opinion to the Business team in respect of the property ownership, encumbrances and compliance with respect to the applicable laws;
* Coordinating with concerned persons of verticals from the various divisions and other stakeholders PAN India for smooth completion of the transactions;
* Drafting, reviewing and finalizing real estate transaction documents such as term sheet/ letter of intent, leave \& license agreements, lease deeds, extension letters, letter of attornment, agreement for sale, sale deeds, etc.;
* Advising the business team on the stamp duty payable on the transaction documents;
* Advising the business team on compliance with the applicable real estate laws, statutes, government regulations and contractual obligations under the transaction documents;
* Periodically preparing and updating the Dashboard summary of the transactions, Status update and the way forward;
* Conduct legal workshops and make presentations to the business teams to provide guidance and training on real estate laws and legal compliance.









**Requisite Qualification\-** 




**Essential\-** 
 Graduate in any discipline with LLB.




**Preferred\-** 
 Mumbai.










**Requisite Experience\-** 




**Essential\-** 
 Advocate having at least 5 years of Real Estate experience.




**Preferred\-** 
 Land Related Litigation.










**Special Skills Required:\-** 




**Essential:** 




 1\. Computer Savvy;




 2\. Knowledge on Land Laws;




 3\. Well conversed with reading of Marathi documents;




 4\. Hands on experience in Real Estate transactions;




 5\. Researching abilities regarding legal issues;




 6\. Excellent drafting skills.

